# Line endings and binary safety.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS (added 2026-07-29)
#
# 1. CHURN. This machine has core.autocrlf=true, and the build scripts in _build/
#    are Perl and write LF. So every time a generator runs, dozens of pages show
#    up as "modified" in GitHub Desktop with zero content changed — 37 of them on
#    29 July, which is enough noise to hide a real change. `* text=auto` settles
#    it: git normalises to LF in the repository and checks out with native endings,
#    so a regenerated file only appears modified when its content actually differs.
#
# 2. BINARIES. With no rules at all, git relies on auto-detection to decide what
#    is text. That is usually right, but "usually" is a poor guarantee for the
#    photographs and PDFs this site is built from — a binary mistaken for text gets
#    its bytes rewritten on checkout and arrives corrupt. The rules below say so
#    explicitly for every binary type in the tree, so it can never be guessed at.
#
# Note for anyone who sees a large one-off diff after this lands: that is the
# normalisation itself, not a content change. `git add --renormalize .` is the
# command that performs it deliberately.

# Default: let git decide text vs binary, and normalise text to LF in the repo.
* text=auto

# Web sources — always text, always LF in the repository.
*.html  text eol=lf
*.htm   text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.pl    text eol=lf
*.pm    text eol=lf
*.htaccess text eol=lf

# Server-side sources - LF, same as every other web source. The mail handlers
# arrived 25 Aug 2026, after this file was written, so they were falling through
# to text=auto and picking up CRLF in the working copy on checkout.
*.php   text eol=lf
*.xml   text eol=lf

# Windows-native helpers must keep CRLF or they misbehave when double-clicked.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Binaries — never transformed, never diffed as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
*.otf   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.mov   binary
*.docx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
